<title>FRANCE: LVMH Q1 turnover jumps 68 pct.</title>
<headline>LVMH Q1 turnover jumps 68 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter to March 31</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					 10,866   vs    6,462</p>
<p>     - Champagne and wine			 1,054   vs	927</p>
<p>     - Cognac and spirits			 1,253   vs    1,147</p>
<p>     - Luggage and fashion			3,080   vs    2,430</p>
<p>     - Luxury goods distribution		5,456   vs    1,859</p>
<p>     - Other					     23   vs	 99</p>
<p>Note - LVMH said first-quarter turnover rose 68 percent from the same year-earlier period, driven by acquisition of 61 percent of U.S. duty free chain DFS. On a like-for-like basis, sales growth was 10.4 percent.</p>
<p>Champagne sales rose 14 percent during the first quarter. &quot;Volume growth was significant, particularly in the U.S. market,&quot; LVMH said. Cognac sales rose nine percent with volumes up seven percent, helped by growth in the U.S. market.</p>
<p>Sales of luggage and leather goods rose by 34 percent, driven by luggage maker Louis Vuitton Malletier. Turnover in luxury goods distribution came mainly from incorporating 3.58 billion francs in DFS sales.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
